00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:14.820
Some of the challenges that we
faced with this online format

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:18.553
is that over Zoom you know the
audio usually is not synced up,

00:04:18.553 --> 00:04:20.220
so trying to choreograph
and collaborate

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.980
is pretty difficult. And
I guess the concept we're

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:26.610
trying to do is like a
Zoom call dance video,

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:28.193
and so we had like
a restricted space,

00:04:28.193 --> 00:04:30.527
and we had to dance mostly
our hands, which is something

00:04:30.527 --> 00:04:31.980
that we're not really used to.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:34.020
And another question is
how do we showcase this,

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:37.380
because you know usually
Ridonkulous, for example,

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.750
hosts a showcase called
Footwork in the spring, which

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:44.150
unfortunately got canceled,
but more on that later.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.290
But some of the
benefits of this format

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:49.080
are that you can have different
takes and put together

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:51.773
different sections, and you
can have interesting screen

00:04:51.773 --> 00:04:53.690
formational ideas, have
different backgrounds,

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:57.540
and props, et cetera
to convey your ideas.

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:00.840
So to talk about a little bit
more about the showcase aspect.

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:03.960
So Movementality
decided basically

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:06.750
to host a showcase in mid-April,
kind of around the same time

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:08.640
that Footwork was
supposed to happen

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:12.240
as a way to try to get the
dance community together.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.880
So on the left you can see
there's a Zoom call here,

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:18.270
where everyone's sort of
watching, and here on the right

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:19.672
is the Facebook event.

00:05:19.672 --> 00:05:21.630
And some of the challenges
with organizing this

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:23.550
was first deciding
whether we want

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:25.260
to do it live or pre-recorded.

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:26.760
We ended up going
with pre-recorded,

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:28.385
just because it was
logistically easier

00:05:28.385 --> 00:05:29.980
and having like a
YouTube playlist.

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:32.010
Then we had to
figure out like how--

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:36.390
who has the best ping and
reliable video playback

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:39.990
and how to deal with
audience response

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:41.615
while the video is being played.

00:05:41.615 --> 00:05:42.990
But then some of
the benefits are

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:44.310
that you get attendance
[? admissions ?] all

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.185
over the country, seeing
like a lot of people

00:05:46.185 --> 00:05:48.130
show up from west
coast and stuff.

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:50.340
And one thing is fun, because
people aren't actually

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:52.020
